Rumsfeld the Ninja has had some lucky breaks of late, making
him the best game I've had in a while.  I've been playing
nethack for just under a year now and have only recently gotten
to a point where I can make it through the early game without
dying from some stupid mistake or other; I know nothing of the game
past Medusa's lair (my two best games were both Valkyries, one of which
died on her quest, the other right after Medusa).

I accidentally hit 'y' at the beginning of this game and got a lawful
Samurai.  I've never played a Samurai before, but this one seems to
be awfully lucky.  Two magic lamps in Minetown yielded a +2 GDSM and
+2 gauntlets of power.  A wand of create monster from the mines
had enough charges to convince Amaterasu Omikami to gift me Snickersnee 
(the Minetown altar was co-aligned).  I also found a unicorn horn and
a luckstone on the first level of the mines, and a (so far unused) wand 
of polymorph on Dlvl 2 or 3.  I killed a shopkeeper for cash and his 
wand of striking, but a cockatrice corpse "partially absolved" me.  I'm
expert in longsword and basic in twoweaponing, Exp level 9, and the 
Grey-Elf I just killed was carrying a +2 elven shield, bringing my AC to 
-12 (cloak of displacement, too).

I'm planning now to head back up to Minetown (I fell through a trap 
door) to ID some potions I'm carrying and bless the unicorn horn and 
luckstone, then do Sokoban and hope for a BoH.  No scrolls of enchant 
weapon or armor yet, either.  Any suggestions?


